# CampusFlow file submissions — manual REST Client flows.
# Set @base, then run Login to populate @token before the calls below.
@base = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
@assignmentId = <assignment-id>

### Login as student
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@institution.edu",
  "password": "Student@123"
}

### Submit a PDF with comments (multipart)
POST {{base}}/submissions/assignments/{{assignmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cf-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="comments"

My solution attached
--cf-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="solution.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./solution.pdf
--cf-boundary--

### Submit notes only (no file)
POST {{base}}/submissions/assignments/{{assignmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cf-boundary

--cf-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="comments"

https://example.com/my-work
--cf-boundary--

### List my submissions
GET {{base}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
